4. OpenCV Image Preprocessing ⭐⭐⭐

img = cv2.resize(img, self.target_size)

img = cv2.bilateralFilter(
    img, d=9,
    sigmaColor=75,
    sigmaSpace=75
)

lab = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2LAB)

lab[:, :, 0] = self.clahe.apply(
    lab[:, :, 0]
)

img = img.astype(np.float32) / 255.0

Explanation

Prepares images before they enter the CNN.

Resizes every image to 224×224.

Removes image noise using a bilateral filter.

Uses CLAHE to improve image contrast.

Normalizes pixels from 0–255 to 0–1.

Gives the CNN consistent and cleaner input.



