5. CNN Architecture ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Input: 224 × 224 × 3

Conv2D(32)
    ↓
BatchNormalization
    ↓
MaxPooling

Conv2D(64)
    ↓
BatchNormalization
    ↓
MaxPooling

Conv2D(128)
    ↓
BatchNormalization
    ↓
MaxPooling

Conv2D(256)
    ↓
BatchNormalization
    ↓
GlobalAveragePooling

Dense(256)
    ↓
Dropout(0.5)

Dense(128)
    ↓
Dropout(0.3)

Dense(5, activation="softmax")

Explanation

This is the main AI model.

Input is an RGB image of 224×224×3.

Convolution layers progressively learn visual features.

32 filters learn basic edges and textures.

64 and 128 filters learn more complex layer patterns.

256 filters learn higher-level defect patterns.

Batch Normalization improves training stability.

MaxPooling reduces the spatial size of feature maps.

Global Average Pooling reduces the extracted features.

Dense layers perform the final classification.

Dropout helps reduce overfitting.

Softmax produces probabilities for all 5 classes.


Simple Viva Explanation

> “The deeper the CNN goes, the more complex the features it learns. The early layers detect edges and textures, while the deeper layers recognize patterns associated with printing defects.”




