8. Defect Prediction ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

probs = self.model.predict(img_batch)[0]

pred_idx = np.argmax(probs)

return {
    "defect_class": DEFECT_CLASSES[pred_idx],
    "confidence": float(probs[pred_idx]),
    "is_defective":
        DEFECT_CLASSES[pred_idx] != "NORMAL"
}

Explanation

Sends a processed image into the trained CNN.

CNN produces probabilities for all five classes.

argmax() selects the class with the highest probability.

Returns:

Defect type

Confidence score

Whether the print is defective

Probability of every class



Example

NORMAL       → 0.04
WARPING      → 0.87  ← Highest
STRINGING    → 0.05
LAYER_SHIFT  → 0.02
CLOGGING     → 0.02

Result → WARPING, 87% confidence


